## Migration Patterns Established

[Conventions for how schema changes happen in this project. Examples:]

- **Backward-compatible patterns:** Add columns nullable first, populate in separate migration, make non-null in a third migration.
- **Type changes:** Through new column rather than alter; copy data; cut over; drop old.
- **Dropping columns:** Soft-deprecate first (stop writing, stop reading), then drop after a deprecation window.
- **Lock duration awareness:** [Conventions about acceptable lock duration in production; off-hours migration windows if applicable.]

